    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know i should talk to someone or whatever but it just feels so pointless. like, if the core of who i was is dead, what's even left to fix? it’s not just a bad mood. it’s like the entire foundation of my life has been erased. how do you even \"rebuild\" when there's nothing left to build on?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When the foundation feels erased, the goal shifts from rebuilding to simply *being* in the present moment, even if it feels empty. You don't have to fix the whole structure at once; small, manageable acts of self-care are the new starting blocks. A therapist can help you explore what remains—the resilience, the capacity for new feelings, or the quiet parts of yourself that haven't been defined by your old achievements. Small steps toward grounding yourself can slowly allow you to see what new possibilities might emerge.",
      "source": "target",
